{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#|jupiter|sandbox|node-tests'\"\\\\.js|cljd_agg|test:sub dao.stream' docs/agents/build-n-test.md && rg -n '\"'^#|segment-matches'\"\\\\?|address-directed' docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md\"","aggregated_output":"5:# BUILD & TEST\n7:## Commands\n10:# Tests (Babashka runner)\n14:# One lane alone: <task>:clj, <task>:cljs, <task>:cljd\n24:# Slow tests: tag a deftest ^:slow. The JVM runner then excludes it from `bb test:clj`.\n25:# Node and Dart have no tag filter, so a .cljc slow test also wraps its body in\n26:# (dao.test-slow/guard \"name\" (fn [] ...)); it prints SKIP unless DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1.\n27:# Node and Dart select slow tests by NAMESPACE (derived by grepping `slow/guard`\n28:# under test/), so the non-slow tests inside those namespaces also run there.\n29:# On Node, shadow also runs the test namespaces those nine require (about\n30:# seven more, e.g. lower-portable-test); on Dart only the nine namespaces run.\n31:# Run test:slow / test:all before a big merge or a commit that touches many parts.\n32:# Run one Dart lane at a time per machine (the limit is cores and the Flutter cache,\n33:# not subsystems). On the many-core remote hosts see \"Remote test servers\" below for\n34:# which lanes may overlap.\n35:#\n36:# When to tag a test slow: when it takes more than about 5 s on any lane (the\n37:# Python e2e tests sit on a ~3 s floor, so their JVM cut is 3.0 s). The\n38:# default lanes must stay in minutes; 22 JVM tests (0.75% of the suite) were\n39:# 81% of its test time. Tag it ^:slow on the JVM; if it is a .cljc test, also\n40:# wrap its body in dao.test-slow/guard so Node and Dart skip it by default. A\n41:# test that is slow only on Dart (dao.jing.dht-test/unproven-chunks-... takes\n42:# 72 s there, 3.6 s on the JVM) is a candidate for a speed investigation first.\n43:# Python slow set (2026-10-06): 65 ^:slow and 15 guard-only tests in the\n44:# yang.python.antlr e2e, e2e-c1, prelude-parity, safepoint, float-address\n45:# and int-contract tests; a Python slice landing runs `bb test:sub:clj yang.python --slow`\n46:# (or `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <ns>`).\n47:# While iterating, use the Gate Ladder (see below): G0 iterate via `bb test:sub:clj <own>`\n48:# or `clojure -M:test -n <ns>`. Do not run the full `bb test` while iterating.\n49:# When a test fails, reproduce and fix it by running ONLY the failing test\n50:# (`clojure -M:test -n <ns> -v <ns>/<var>`, Node `--test=<ns>`, Dart `--only <ns>`) --\n51:# never the whole suite (owner ruling 2026-11-01; see Gate Ladder G0).\n52:# Individual tests run fine on the laptop; suite-scale runs (G1 subsystem sets,\n53:# G2 changed sets, full suites, slow tier, nightly) run on shiva/jupiter --\n54:# the suite has outgrown the laptop (owner ruling 2026-11-04).\n55:# At slice checkpoints, run G1 (`bb test:sub <own>`). Before landing a slice, run\n56:# G2 (`bb test:changed` in the worktree across all three lanes).\n57:# Full repo-wide `bb test` runs once daily on the remote hosts (04:00 VN);\n58:# a MERGE needs only the affected tests (bb test:changed) -- owner ruling 2026-11-01;\n59:# for a fix branch, the previously-failing tests green IS the merge bar\n60:# (owner ruling 2026-11-07; see Gate Ladder G0).\n61:# Cross-host bugs show only on Node or Dart, so tri-host verification is mandatory\n62:# for every gate from G1 upward. Run one lane set at a time per machine to avoid\n63:# contention (a laptop has 8 cores; the 24- and 48-core remote hosts have room to\n64:# overlap lanes, see \"Remote test servers\" below).\n65:# Measured fast-lane times (2026-10-03): bb test about 14 min = JVM 5.5 + Node\n66:# 3.8 + Dart 4.3, plus builds. test:slow: Node and Dart about 5 min each (mostly\n67:# compile); the JVM half is estimated at 17 min (long-loops-test alone is 14),\n68:# not yet run end to end. test:all: JVM 20+ min, also an estimate.\n71:# Cross-host peers the JVM lane spawns. `bb test` builds both. A bare\n72:# `bb test:clj` builds only the Node REPL (it depends on build:yin-repl-node);\n73:# without build:yin-repl-peer first, the Dart-peer tests skip with a printed notice.\n74:# Under `bb test:sub` and `bb test:changed`, prerequisites are derived automatically.\n82:### Changed-only tests: `bb test:changed`\n104:### Sharded quick JVM feedback and change routing\n205:jupiter 5,645 s at 12 workers, shiva comparable). Do not run another lane\n208:#### Worktree-local prerequisite caches\n244:### Subsystem-first tests: `bb test:sub`\n260:#### Canonical Subsystems (`src/dev/subsystems.edn`)\n273:#### Gate Ladder (docs/design/test.subsystems.md)\n279:   deftest: add `-v <ns>/<var-name>`). Node: `node target/node-tests.js --test=<ns>`\n281:   Dart: `bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only <ns>[/<test-name>]` (owner ruling\n338:# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\n343:# ClojureDart\n346:# Linting\n350:The Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\n372:## Test tiers: quick and slow\n394:  disjoint lane pair (`src/dev/nightly.clj`): **jupiter takes the jvm lane, shiva\n396:  jupiter reads it and falls back to its own current master as an advisory run).\n414:| Full JVM lane, sharded by subsystem, before tagging (jupiter, 13 shards, 8 at a time) | 46.5 min, set by `yin.repl.python-antlr-test` |\n415:| **Quick tier, sharded by subsystem (jupiter, same 13 shards)** | **5 min 3 s**, 4055 tests, all shards exit 0; longest shards `yang.python` 253 s and `yin.vm.ucf` 204 s |\n430:# timing.clj: require the namespace, for each deftest var that is not ^:slow:\n431:#   (binding [clojure.test/*test-out* (java.io.StringWriter.)] (clojure.test/test-vars [v]))\n432:# and print the elapsed nanoseconds. One-off setup (a `use-fixtures :once` or a parser\n433:# load) is paid by the first test in file order; check before tagging that test alone.\n442:#!/usr/bin/env bash\n443:# Usage: shard-jvm.sh <clone> [parallel]  -- JVM lane sharded by subsystem (fast tests, -e :slow)\n463:# coverage: every JVM test namespace under test/ vs the union of the shards\n482:#!/usr/bin/env bash\n483:# Usage: slow-tier.sh <clone> [parallel] -- the ^:slow tests of the tagged namespaces, one JVM per namespace\n502:## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n511:| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). mise was moved off the apt package to the official user-local install (`~/.local/bin/mise`, 2026.11.2, owner action 2026-11-07) so both hosts share shiva's layout; toolchains in `~/.local/share/mise/installs/` were untouched. Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n513:### Peer dispatch: check the loads, route to the lower-loaded host\n515:shiva and jupiter are **peers**, not a primary and a spare (owner ruling\n516:2026-11-15, superseding the earlier \"leave jupiter out, use shiva\" routing).\n517:jupiter has the larger core budget (48 vs 24). Before dispatching any\n523:for h in shiva.stigmergy.systems jupiter.stigmergy.systems; do\n530:work. If the loads are comparable, prefer jupiter (more cores). Two\n532:keeps jupiter=JVM / shiva=node+dart because the lanes are sharded and\n541:### Gate log hygiene: per-run directories, never shared per-lane logs (2026-11-14 incident)\n548:(yang.php branch-tip gate, jupiter): the yang.php lane failed with\n558:# per-gate run dir; the summaries live beside the detail logs\n564:bb test:sub dao.stream > \"\\$RUN\"/dao-stream.out 2>&1\n576:### Kill remote processes by exact PID, never by name pattern\n591:### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n600:# once per host: a separate scratch clone, not the working copy\n612:### A clone is only current if it updated from real master\n638:### Activate the toolchain in the right order\n645:export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\n657:### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\n664:average over 100 on 2026-11-01; the remote hosts own that tier. On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\n695:join. A single-lane invocation (jupiter's `jvm`) is unchanged: one clone,\n697:command line (shiva: `node,dart` + `--pin-publish`; jupiter: `jvm` +\n700:### Scratch-clone first-run gaps (two measured sightings)\n733:### Merge verification: run the suite from a fresh clone, not the authoring worktree\n754:### Ledger commit hygiene: never commit a conflict marker\n775:### The jolt J2 lane: run it with `--jobs` on the servers\n782:(strictly serial), which on jupiter makes the full ~179-namespace lane a\n789:  sit far inside jupiter's 48 cores / 62 GB and shiva's 24 / 62;\n809:### The full run\n819:#!/usr/bin/env bash\n820:# ~/ci/run-full.sh <jvm-node-clone> [<dart-clone>]   (both hosts run all three lanes; a second clone for Dart is recommended)\n841:    lane dart bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj ) &\n859:### Known differences from the laptop\n879:### The nightly full suite and the branch-testing rule (2026-10-30 owner ruling)\n890:  shiva and jupiter, hourly cron plus a 04:00 Vietnam guard and flock,\n893:  the JVM full suite on jupiter, the full Node and Dart suites on shiva.\n919:built on. Concretely: `bb test:sub dao.stream` (the subsystem's tests,\n926:### Measured times (first runs, 2026-10-11, commit 84c7c9b7, all lanes concurrent)\n937:### Jupiter verification run (2026-10-29, commit 7c0a078f, scratch clone, sequential lanes)\n939:First full tri-host verification of jupiter. Prerequisites (npm ci, Node REPL,\n949:taken-port/bind-failed signature recorded above). Routing summary: jupiter\n963:### Remote agent execution (delegate CLIs on shiva and jupiter)\n1003:the full tri-host suite (jupiter verified 2026-10-29 — see Measured times;\n1007:## Testing Philosophy & TDD\n1020:## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n1:# Multihash-Style Content Addressing for DaoJing and yin.vm\n5:## Decision\n24:## Address format\n45:## Invariants\n51:- Verification is address-directed; minting primitives are not validators.\n63:## DaoJing design\n65:### Closed algorithm registry\n98:### Public digest primitives\n120:### `canonical-bytes`\n139:### `content-hash`\n168:### `segment-key`\n193:### Address parsing\n227:### `segment-matches?`\n232:(segment-matches? address payload)\n246:Malformed, unsupported, noncanonical, or mismatched addresses return false. Canonical-encoder refusal also returns false, making `segment-matches?` a total verification predicate. Minting operations such as `materialize!` and `segment-key` continue to throw on encoder refusal.\n250:### `materialize!`\n269:(segment-matches? address stored)\n283:### `get`\n293:`get` need not rehash every successful read. Existing backend insertion and replay checks, plus higher-level verified readers, retain their responsibilities. A consumer that verifies fetched content uses `segment-matches?`.\n300:### File-backend codec round-trip (historical, registry era)\n309:It does not use `segment-matches?`. Both sides must be hashed with the algorithm selected for the pending address:\n318:## Clean introduction\n334:## Call-site audit and required dispositions\n345:### Explicit hash contracts\n359:### Primitive-profile identifier\n371:### DaoSpace schema identity\n384:(jing/segment-matches? schema-address schema)\n389:### Address-directed validation sites\n391:The following sites validate content against an address already supplied by stored data, a caller, or a peer. They use `segment-matches?` (the `dao.jing.remote` sites describe the code as it stands today; `dao.jing.remote` is deprecated whole and its successor `dao.jing.content` keeps the same checks, per `dao.stream.remote.md` section 8):\n413:Backend sites currently compare `segment-hash` with `content-hash`; DaoSpace and yin.vm sites generally re-mint with one-argument `segment-key` and compare whole addresses. Both mechanisms incorrectly substitute minting defaults for address-directed verification.\n417:### Address-directed mint sites\n439:### Documentation-only SHA assumptions\n445:## yin.vm H and R disposition\n466:## Host libraries\n480:### Maintenance risks\n497:## Sequencing with canonical CBOR\n536:## Phased rollout\n538:### H0: contract and evidence\n555:- malformed, unknown-algorithm, noncanonical-spelling, wrong-length, uppercase, encoder-refusal (returning false for `segment-matches?`), and EDN round-trip cases are specified;\n559:### H1: registry and whole-system cutover\n574:- all validation sites in the complete audit use `segment-matches?`;\n587:### H2: multi-algorithm verification and hardening\n606:- addresses minted under explicit `{:algorithm :sha256}` continue to verify correctly via `segment-matches?` without depending on or altering `default-hash-algorithm`;\n608:- `dao.jing.md` states: \"Verification must be address-directed; minting primitives are not validators\";\n614:## Test obligations\n641:## Explicit non-goals\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat collab/yang-php/1795098934000-from-yangclojure-master-red-store-write-allowlist.md && sed -n '1,115p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator.cljc && sed -n '680,730p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc && sed -n '280,330p' src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc && sed -n '450,490p' test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc && cat test/yin/vm/code_entry_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat collab/yang-php/1795098934000-from-yangclojure-master-red-store-write-allowlist.md && sed -n '1,115p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator.cljc && sed -n '680,730p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc && sed -n '280,330p' src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc && sed -n '450,490p' test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc && cat test/yin/vm/code_entry_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-19 14:35:34 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-19 21:35:34 +0700\nFrom: yang.clojure orchestrator seat\nTo: yang.php / DRY orchestrator seat\n\n# FYI: master is RED — two lint failures from the r18 landing (aa174a11 / 657f01ff)\n\nVerified on jupiter (scratch clone, focused runs on origin/master 657f01ff AND on\nour branch after merging master — identical on both, so pre-existing, not ours):\n\n1. `yin.vm.store-write-audit-test/every-store-mutation-is-on-the-allowlist`\n   — `src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_coordinator.cljc` added\n   `[\"compile-and-publish*!\" :map] 1` to the source-sites map but the test's\n   allowlist was not updated with the entry + reason.\n2. `dao.jing.hash-registry-contract-test/architectural-lint-sweeps-production-sources`\n   — flags `src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc` code-entry-handler for a forbidden\n   equality validation against dao.jing default minting vars (`(not= address (:address entry))`\n   chain). This one may predate r18 — please confirm ownership.\n\nEvidence: ~/ci/logs/fixorder-g2-20261119-043834/{master-redcheck.out,branch-mergecheck.out}\non jupiter. Our full-tri-host gate run also caught these (bbtest.out in the same dir).\n\nThe yang.clojure fix branch (fix/constructed-collection-order @ 7e6d720c) is\nclean modulo these two. Please land the allowlist/lint fix so master goes green.\n(ns yang.php.antlr.eval-coordinator\n  \"Composition-supplied eval frontend and stream service.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yang.antlr.packet :as packet]\n            [yang.php.antlr.cst :as cst]\n            [yang.php.antlr.eval-admission :as admission]\n            [yang.php.antlr.eval-publication :as publication]\n            [yang.php.antlr.eval-transport :as transport]\n            [yang.php.antlr.scope :as scope]\n            [yang.php.antlr.siteset :as siteset]))\n\n\n(defn make-worker\n  []\n  (cst/make-eval-worker))\n\n\n(defn compile-request\n  \"Prepare one request for later eval-unit emission. Identity includes the\n   complete request (including bytes and caller-supplied revisions/options),\n   the source goal, grammar and admission profile. No caller runtime state is\n   needed by this service.\"\n  [worker request]\n  (let [{:keys [source] :as admitted} (admission/admit-request request)]\n    (if-not source\n      admitted\n      (let [pk (cst/parse-source worker (:yang.compile/unit request) source)\n            identity {:request request\n                      :yang.php/source (:yang.php/source request)\n                      :yang.php.eval/profile-revision admission/profile-revision\n                      :yang.php/source-goal :eval\n                      :yang.php/grammar cst/grammar-id}]\n        (if (:yang.php/not-php pk)\n          {:request request :identity identity :cst pk}\n          (let [validated (packet/validate! pk {:source source})]\n            (cond-> {:request request :identity identity :cst validated}\n              (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome validated))\n              (assoc :scope (scope/analyze validated)))))))))\n\n\n(defn compile-transport-request\n  \"Validate a sealed transport request before handing it to the parser worker.\n   Refusals include the request identity only when it is portable data.\"\n  [worker request]\n  (if-let [defect (transport/request-defect request)]\n    (cond-> {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/rejected\n             :yang.compile/reason :yang.compile/invalid-request\n             :yang.compile/detail defect}\n      (and (map? request) (contains? request :yang.compile/request)\n           (transport/portable-data? (:yang.compile/request request)))\n      (assoc :yang.compile/request (:yang.compile/request request)))\n    (compile-request worker request)))\n\n\n(defn- compile-and-publish*!\n  \"Compile a sealed request and publish its canonical module and occurrence\n   set to the composition's store. Linker admission is a separate step.\"\n  [{:keys [worker store registry stage-requirement]} request]\n  (let [{:keys [cst identity] :as prepared} (compile-transport-request worker request)\n        correlation (transport/correlation request)]\n    (cond\n      (:yang.compile/outcome prepared) prepared\n      (not= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome cst))\n      (transport/rejected request :yang.compile/invalid-source\n                          {:yang.compile/diagnostics (:yang.cst/errors cst)})\n      :else\n      (let [name (symbol (str \"eval.\" (name (jing/segment-key identity))))\n            result (publication/publish! store registry name prepared)]\n        (if (= :ok (:status result))\n          (let [address (:address result)\n                site (:sites result)\n                stage (when stage-requirement\n                        (siteset/stage registry stage-requirement\n                                       {address [(:record-address site)]}))\n                derived (when stage (stage {:store store :datoms [] :principals []}\n                                           name address))]\n            (if (and derived (not= :ok (:status derived)))\n              (transport/rejected request :yang.compile/derivation-failed\n                                  {:yang.compile/detail derived})\n              (merge correlation {:yang.compile/outcome :yang.compile/published\n                                  :yang.compile/module name\n                                  :yang.compile/address address\n                                  :yang.compile/source-address (:source-address result)\n                                  :yang.compile/site-record (:record-address site)}\n                     (when derived {:yang.compile/active-address (:address derived)\n                                    :yang.compile/derivation (:derivation derived)}))))\n          (transport/rejected request :yang.compile/publication-failed\n                              {:yang.compile/detail (select-keys result [:reason :status])}))))))\n\n\n(defn compile-and-publish!\n  \"Compile and publish, returning classified frontend diagnostics to the caller.\"\n  [state request]\n  (try\n    (compile-and-publish*! state request)\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n      (let [diagnostic (ex-data e)]\n        (if (:yang.php/diagnostic diagnostic)\n          (transport/rejected request\n                              (if (= :yang.php/compile-error\n                                     (:yang.php/diagnostic diagnostic))\n                                :yang.compile/invalid-source\n                                :yang.compile/unsupported)\n                              {:yang.compile/diagnostic diagnostic})\n          (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn serve\n  \"Serve at most `budget` requests. Advance the immutable request cursor only\n   after its answer is appended, so a full response stream loses no request.\"\n  ([state] (serve state 32))\n  ([state budget]\n   (loop [state state, remaining budget]\n     (if (not (pos? remaining))\n                                    :yin.link/contract contract}\n                         :request link-request-resource\n                         :response link-response-resource)\n            entry (cond-> entry\n                    minted (assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor minted)))]\n        (block-on state (append-link-request resources entry gate))))))\n\n\n(defn require-handler\n  \"Resolve `:module/require`, raising a refusal at resume.\"\n  [state effect opts]\n  (handle-require state effect opts false))\n\n\n(defn try-require-handler\n  \"Resolve `:module/try-require`, returning linker outcomes as data.\"\n  [state effect opts]\n  (handle-require state effect opts true))\n\n\n(defn code-entry-handler\n  \"Read a declared export from an already installed, address-pinned module.\"\n  [state effect _opts]\n  (let [{:keys [module address export]} effect\n        entry (when (symbol? module) (module-entry (:modules (:modules state)) module))\n        manifest (:manifest entry)\n        reason (cond\n                 (nil? entry) :module-missing\n                 (or (nil? address) (not= address (:address entry))\n                     (not= address (jing/segment-key manifest))\n                     (not= module (:yin.module/name manifest))) :manifest-mismatch\n                 (not (contains? (:yin.module/exports manifest) export)) :export-undeclared\n                 (not (contains? (:bindings entry) export)) :binding-missing)]\n    {:state state, :blocked? false\n     :value (if reason\n              {:status :refused :reason reason :module module :export export}\n              (get (:bindings entry) export))}))\n\n\n(defn code-entry\n  \"Construct an effect to retrieve a previously installed export.\"\n  [module address export]\n  (make-effect :code/entry {:module module :address address :export export}))\n\n\n(defn register-code-module\n  \"Expose the profiled code/entry constructor to a composition.\"\n  [registry]\n  (register-host-module registry 'code {'entry code-entry}\n                        {'entry (vm/primitive-profile 'entry :effectful [3]\n                                                      #{:code/entry} :none)}))\n   Throws on invalid input.\"\n  [address]\n  (if-let [parsed (parse-segment-address address)]\n    (:algorithm parsed)\n    (throw (ex-info \"not a segment content address\" {:address address}))))\n\n\n(defn segment-digest\n  \"The lowercase hex digest carried by a segment address.\n   Throws on invalid input.\"\n  [address]\n  (if-let [parsed (parse-segment-address address)]\n    (:digest parsed)\n    (throw (ex-info \"not a segment content address\" {:address address}))))\n\n\n(defn segment-hash\n  \"The content hash carried by a segment address. Equivalent to segment-digest.\n   Total only over valid segment addresses; throws on invalid input.\"\n  [k]\n  (segment-digest k))\n\n\n(defn segment-matches?\n  \"Total verification predicate: true when address is a valid segment address\n   and its digest matches the hash of canonical-bytes of payload under the\n   address-carried algorithm.\n   Never throws: malformed addresses, unknown algorithms, digest mismatches,\n   and canonical-encoder refusal all return false.\"\n  [address payload]\n  (if-let [{:keys [algorithm digest]} (parse-segment-address address)]\n    (try\n      (let [bs (canonical-bytes payload)\n            actual (digest-bytes algorithm bs)]\n        (= digest actual))\n      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n        false))\n    false))\n\n\n(defn segment-bytes-match?\n  \"Total verification predicate over bytes: true when address is a valid\n   segment address whose digest is the hash of bs under the address-carried\n   algorithm. Never throws: a malformed address, a foreign algorithm, or a\n   non-byte bs all answer false.\"\n  [address bs]\n  (if-let [{:keys [algorithm digest]} (parse-segment-address address)]\n    (try\n      (= digest (digest-bytes algorithm bs))\n      (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n        false))\n            (str \"UTF-8 vector for \" (pr-str string) \" must match\"))))))\n\n\n#?(:cljd nil\n   :clj\n   (deftest architectural-lint-sweeps-production-sources\n     (testing (str \"source sweep: no equality comparison against \"\n                   \"dao.jing default minting vars\")\n       (let [src-dir    (io/file \"src/cljc\")\n             files      (filter #(and (.isFile ^java.io.File %)\n                                      (.endsWith (.getName ^java.io.File %)\n                                                 \".cljc\"))\n                                (file-seq src-dir))\n             exemptions #{\"src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc\"\n                          \"src/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc\"}]\n         (is (pos? (count files)))\n         (doseq [f files\n                 :let [path (.getPath ^java.io.File f)]\n                 :when (not (contains? exemptions path))]\n           (with-open [rdr (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader f))]\n             (let [eof (Object.)]\n               (loop []\n                 (let [form (try\n                              (read {:eof eof\n                                     :read-cond :allow\n                                     :features #{:clj :cljc}}\n                                    rdr)\n                              (catch Exception _ eof))]\n                   (when-not (identical? form eof)\n                     (is (not (flags-equality-validation? form))\n                         (str \"Found forbidden equality validation in \"\n                              path \": \" (pr-str form)))\n                     (recur)))))))))))\n(ns yin.vm.code-entry-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yin.vm.effect :as effect]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(deftest installed-export-is-address-pinned\n  (let [manifest {:yin.module/name 'eval.unit :yin.module/exports #{'entry}}\n        address (jing/segment-key manifest)\n        registry (module/assoc-module (module/default-registry) 'eval.unit\n                                      {:manifest manifest :address address\n                                       :bindings {'entry :callable}})\n        state {:modules registry}\n        effect {:module 'eval.unit :address address :export 'entry}\n        run #(module/code-entry-handler state % {})]\n    (is (= :callable (:value (run effect))))\n    (is (= state (:state (run effect))))\n    (is (false? (:blocked? (run effect))))\n    (doseq [[bad reason] [[(assoc effect :address :wrong) :manifest-mismatch]\n                          [(assoc effect :export 'missing) :export-undeclared]\n                          [(assoc effect :module 'absent) :module-missing]]]\n      (is (= reason (get-in (run bad) [:value :reason]))))\n    (doseq [bad [(assoc effect :address :wrong)\n                 (assoc effect :export 'missing)\n                 (assoc effect :module 'absent)]]\n      (is (= :refused (get-in (run bad) [:value :status]))))\n    (is (= module/code-entry-handler\n           (module/get-effect-handler registry :code/entry)))\n    (is (= {:effect :code/entry :module 'eval.unit :address address :export 'entry}\n           (effect/descriptor (module/code-entry 'eval.unit address 'entry))))\n    (is (fn? (module/resolve-module (module/register-code-module registry) 'code.entry)))\n    (doseq [modified [(assoc-in registry [:modules 'eval 'unit :manifest :extra] true)\n                      (update-in registry [:modules 'eval 'unit] dissoc :bindings)]]\n      (is (= :refused (get-in (module/code-entry-handler (assoc state :modules modified) effect {})\n                              [:value :status]))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
