{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,48p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_publication.cljc && rg -n 'defn overlay|defn read-at|jing/' src/cljc/yang/core/siteset_store.cljc && sed -n '1,63p' test/dao/jing/hash_registry_contract_test.cljc && rg -n 'datagram|tcp|websocket' src/dev/subsystems.edn test/dao/stream/{datagram_test.cljc,ws_project_cross_jvm_test.clj} | head -30\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.eval-publication\n  \"Publish an admitted eval unit and its canonical safepoint occurrences.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n            [yang.php.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(defn publish!\n  \"Publish a prepared, successfully parsed eval unit under the supplied name.\n   Retain the coordinator's identity and bind its site set to the manifest.\"\n  [store registry name prepared]\n  (if (= :yang.cst/ok (get-in prepared [:cst :yang.cst/outcome]))\n    (let [spec (lower/eval-module-spec registry name (:cst prepared)\n                                       {:eval-service? (boolean (module/module-entry (:modules registry)\n                                                                                     'eval.compiler))})\n          result (publish/publish-module! store spec)]\n      (if (= :refused (:status result))\n        result\n        (assoc result :status :ok :identity (:identity prepared)\n               :source-address (jing/materialize! store (:identity prepared))\n               :sites (siteset/publish! store (:address result) (:ast spec)))))\n    {:status :refused :reason :eval-source-not-ready :identity (:identity prepared)}))\n7:(defn read-at\n10:  (when (jing/segment-address? address)\n14:        (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bytes) (jing/segment-value address bytes)))))\n56:(defn overlay\n(ns dao.jing.hash-registry-contract-test\n  \"Phase H0 ('contract and evidence') of the DaoJing multihash\n   content-addressing rollout (docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md,\n   architect signed off:\n   collab/1790147499393-architect-hash-registry-signoff\n   .gpt-5.6-sol.findings.md).\n\n   H0 freezes the address grammar, the total-predicate contract for\n   `segment-matches?`, EDN round-tripping, and the architectural lint\n   target -- before any of it exists in `dao.jing` (reserved for H1). This\n   namespace is therefore self-contained: it defines a *reference*\n   implementation of the frozen grammar/parser/predicate rules as local,\n   private functions, and pins their behavior against:\n\n   - `dao.jing/sha256-bytes`, `dao.jing/canonical-bytes`, and\n     `dao.jing/content-hash`, which are real today and do not change\n     shape in H0 (SHA-256 minting is already what `content-hash`\n     computes); and\n   - the frozen BLAKE3-256 fixtures in\n     test/resources/dao/jing/blake3-vectors.edn and\n     test/resources/dao/jing/digest-table.edn, standing in for a real\n     BLAKE3 provider (none exists until H1's pinned dependencies land).\n\n   When H1 lands the registry in `dao.jing` itself, this namespace's\n   reference `parse-segment-address`/`segment-matches?` are replaced by\n   calls to the real `dao.jing` functions; the fixture data and the\n   specification the tests encode do not change, only which\n   implementation answers them.\"\n  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as jing-cbor]\n            #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as dart-io]]\n                :clj [[clojure.java.io :as io]]))\n  #?@(:cljd [(:import [\"dart:typed_data\" Uint8List])]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Fixture loading (portable text read + clojure.edn/read-string, the same\n;; pattern test/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc uses for its JSON corpus).\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- read-text\n  [path]\n  #?(:cljd (.readAsStringSync (dart-io/File. path))\n     :clj (slurp path)\n     :cljs (.readFileSync (js/require \"fs\") path \"utf8\")))\n\n\n(def ^:private blake3-vectors*\n  (delay (edn/read-string\n           (read-text \"test/resources/dao/jing/blake3-vectors.edn\"))))\n\n\n(def ^:private digest-table*\n  (delay (edn/read-string\n           (read-text \"test/resources/dao/jing/digest-table.edn\"))))\n\n\n(defn- blake3-vectors\n  []\n  @blake3-vectors*)\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:1:(ns dao.stream.datagram-test\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:2:  \"Portable, host-free tests for dao.stream.datagram\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:3:   (docs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md): the value shapes of section 2, the\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:8:   dao.stream.datagram.{jvm,node,dart} drive over real sockets; everything\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:14:            [dao.stream.datagram :as datagram]\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:53:  {:dao.stream.datagram/destination {:dao.stream.datagram/host host\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:54:                                     :dao.stream.datagram/port port}})\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:61:         :dao.stream.datagram/bytes\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:67:   `:sends` records every datagram the seam was handed as\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:83:                        deposit (datagram/send-failed-event id \"scripted refusal\"))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:85:                       :dao.stream.datagram/reason \"scripted refusal\"})\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:90:                        (stream/append! deposit (datagram/closed-event id))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:102:    (stream/append! deposit (datagram/bound-event id \"127.0.0.1\" 41234))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:103:    (datagram/writer seam\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:104:                     {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/datagram\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:106:                      :dao.stream.datagram/bind-host \"127.0.0.1\"\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:107:                      :dao.stream.datagram/bind-port 41234}\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:108:                     (or max-bytes datagram/default-max-bytes))))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:123:      (is (datagram/ip-literal? valid) (pr-str valid)))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:145:      (is (not (datagram/ip-literal? invalid)) (pr-str invalid)))))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:150:    (is (datagram/valid-port? valid) (pr-str valid)))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:152:    (is (not (datagram/valid-port? invalid)) (pr-str invalid))))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:162:    (is (= {:dao.stream.datagram/socket \"s1\"\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:163:            :dao.stream.datagram/event :dao.stream.datagram/bound\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:164:            :dao.stream.datagram/local {:dao.stream.datagram/host \"127.0.0.1\"\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:165:                                        :dao.stream.datagram/port 41234}}\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:166:           (datagram/bound-event \"s1\" \"127.0.0.1\" 41234)))\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:167:    (is (= {:dao.stream.datagram/socket \"s1\"\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:168:            :dao.stream.datagram/event :dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed\ntest/dao/stream/datagram_test.cljc:169:            :dao.stream.datagram/reason \"port in use\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
